    <briefdescription>
<para>The <ref refid="namespace_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_n_s_n_i" kindref="compound">NSNI</ref> stabilization of the displacement rows of a particle, shared by the displacement and the gradient-enhanced particles (whose dofs of a node start with the displacement). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The stabilization adds to the force of node <formula id="33">$ A $</formula> the term  <formula id="263">$ D_{iK}\, \partial \tau_{ij} /
\partial Y_K $</formula>, with the moment-weighted second gradient of the test function    <formula id="264">\[  D_{iK} = \frac{\partial Y_j}{\partial x_i}\, \frac{\partial^2 T_A}{\partial Y_j \partial Y_L}\,
  \frac{M^Y_{LK}}{J_Y} ,
\]</formula> the second moments <formula id="265">$ \boldsymbol{M}^Y $</formula> of the particle domain and  <formula id="266">$ J_Y = \det \partial\boldsymbol{Y} /
\partial\boldsymbol{X} $</formula>. The second gradients of the shape functions are the smoothed ones of the particle domain, <formula id="267">$ \partial^2 N_B / \partial Y_I \partial Y_J $</formula> from the face sums <computeroutput>d2N_dYdY[J](I, B)</computeroutput> of <formula id="268">$ \partial N_B / \partial Y_I\, n_J\, dA / V $</formula>, symmetrized. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
